{
  "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
  "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0000-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "LISA S. BLATT, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner. CHRISTOPHER G. MICHEL, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner. JOSEPH R. PALMORE, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Atlantic Richfield Company)",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case involves whether the hundreds of thousands of landowners on Superfund sites can bring state lawsuits to implement their own piecemeal hazardous waste cleanups. The answer should be no."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Atlantic Richfield Company)",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court should reverse for three reasons. First, Section 113 bars Respondents' challenge to EPA's remedy. Second, Section 122 bars Respondents from undertaking any remedial actions absent EPA's authorization. And, third, a restoration remedy is preempted because it would require Atlantic Richfield to effectuate the very cleanup that federal law prohibits the company from doing on its own, and a restoration remedy would prevent EPA from carrying out its statutory mandate to implement comprehensive cleanups."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Ms. Blatt, same kind of question, and maybe it goes to a bunch of your arguments. I mean, look, if I were writing this statute, I would say it all goes to the EPA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0000-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, to go to some of the questions that have -- have been raised already, this is a narrow -- our argument here is narrow. The -- the statute does have savings clauses, and we don't dispute that Respondents can move forward with their claims for money damages under state law and nuisance and tort and other related theories that don't call into question the EPA remedy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Sorry, are you agreeing with Ms. Blatt that your plan is both the floor and the ceiling?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So are you reading their state -- are you reading this remedy as requiring the remediation that's awarded no matter what? With or without EPA approval?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Michel",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MICHEL: So I think two responses. First, I do want to make clear that 122(e)(6), the PRP provision that we're talking about here, only applies to remedial action. And that has a defined statutory definition. It's in 9601(a)(4)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Then -- then what is your answer to the question Ms. Blatt was asked?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Michel",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MICHEL: I agree with you, Justice Ginsburg. You could resolve the case by -- by saying that Respondents are PRPs who need EPA authorization -- authorization and don't have it and, therefore, their -- their claim fails."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, it did -- it did, Mr. Palmore, but, under your theory, how would you decide whether somebody is a potentially responsible party? It sounds like you would need a court adjudication to do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So you're saying that even in the absence of the statute of limitations issue, these would not be potentially responsible parties because the government is subject to a kind of estoppel principle?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They are -- they -- they own land that contains hazardous substances. I thought that potentially responsible parties are people who own land, whether they have any fault or not, but their land does contain hazardous substances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I go back to Justice Kagan's question for a second? If EPA notified landowners early on that they were all PRPs, and you disagreed, how would that be resolved?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would you think it would be an appropriate rule if basically it were up to EPA to designate potentially responsible parties or at least that there were a strong presumption that, if EPA designated somebody as a potentially responsible party, they were one?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem, knowing your land -- your clients are landowners of land that is polluted, and it's a Superfund site."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Maybe it was a moot question if it's your obligation to ask them, meaning, if you are a PRP and that's what we conclude, it would be your obligation to ask them for permission."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you be specific about what EPA could do to take care of its interests in that scenario?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I guess the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. PALMORE",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PALMORE: Well, EPA is, of course, all over this site, and it can enforce the law here. The question is whether we are -- should be similarly situated to just you and me and any American who, if we violate the law, the regulator, the law enforcement, can come after us, or whether we have this kind of superintending presence of agency authority over us and our private property for the rest of our lives."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. PALMORE",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e58893b1e61686fb302f008ad68edf44d0ee65dd231b2b41116b8e47e62514bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e58893b1e616-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PALMORE: Your Honor, there's no evidence that Congress intended this obscure corner of Section 122 about settlements to give EPA that kind of vast control forever over private property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1498",
      "confidence": 0.0,
